# Sentron panel overflows phone widths — real-device report from Will

Coordinate: 15.6.8/8.6.10/6.5.6
Issued: 2026-11-08 21:34 CST
Request (verbatim): This is not mobile friendly...
Status: complete 2026-11-08 23:02 — PR #36 open against exo; merge is Will's

Notes:
- Will's real-phone screenshot (2026-11-08 21:34): the Sentron panel clips at the right edge — the coordinate header line and the SBOR Signatures lines run off-screen ('Human + Sentier…'). NOT covered by the mobile fixes (PR #34): the emulation pass's checklist opened Nav but never Sentron on a phone profile — a scoping miss in the test pass Emise commissioned. Fix: panel content fits 360–430px with nothing truncated; Sentron itself in the verification shots this time.
- DESIGN DIRECTION (Will, 2026-11-08 21:37, verbatim): 'on mobile, just use a coordinate address, buttons and make the editor use as much real estate as possible.' Builder re-briefed same evening: mobile layout = compact bar (coordinate address + buttons), editor maximized, Nav/Sentron as full-width tap-open sheets; desktop unchanged. PR #34 interaction analysis required in the new PR's body (which of its fixes still apply; whether its landscape wrap goes moot).
- RECOVERY (2026-11-08 22:2x): the original builder was killed by a runtime restart mid-verification; its work survived on disk (modified source + PR body + verify workspace in ~/workspace/sentron-mobile-fit/). A recovery builder is porting the design onto current exo a02e0e1b — which now includes #6's landed phone layout — with explicit reconciliation against #6, then verification, branch + PR. Stray before-server on aletheia:8904 confirmed dead.

Results:
- RECOVERED + LANDED AS PR #36 (branch emise/sentron-mobile-fit, 4 commits on exo a02e0e1b): the original builder's 4 commits were intact (byte-identical to its node branch, never pushed); the recovery hand-ported the design onto current exo, unified on #6's 760px breakpoint and drawer mechanism — ported on top: coordinate+buttons actions row + message strip in the top bar, panels widened to full-viewport sheets with in-panel close, status bar hidden at rest as a 'More' bottom sheet, sheet content-fit rules. Never-regress set verified (#34 x5, #12, #8 demo probed live 200, #31 slot, #32 art, footer). Tests 235 passed, identical to pristine-exo baseline.
- Emulation verification (Android 412x915, iOS 390x844, 360x740, desktop 1400x900; portrait + landscape): zero console errors, zero horizontal spill in every measured state; sheets exactly viewport width; all 13 More-sheet items reachable. Editor area grew from removing exo's permanently-wrapped phone footer: 514->761px Android, 443->638px iOS, 315->534px narrow. The SBOR Signatures scroll from Will's photograph renders complete at 360px — no truncated lines. Evidence: ~/workspace/sentron-mobile-fit/verify/ + PORT-NOTES.md. Flags: (1) PRE-EXISTING desktop bug found — signed-in status bar overflows a 1400px viewport on pristine exo too (Claim dashboard + sign-out past the edge); noted in the PR body, not fixed here. (2) Sponsor slot verified by CSS parity + tests only (renders only when configured). Emulation caveat stands: real-device check is the last word.
