# Build state machine review into MOAT

Coordinate: 19.6.8/9.6.15/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 13:19 CST
Request (verbatim): build state machine review into MOAT, specifically (on Steve Ruiz's 'find all of the implicit state machines in my app', posted in MOAT deliberately; Will: never assume I post in the wrong channel by accident)
Status: complete 2026-11-07

Notes:
- Scope per Will's correction: NOT a hunt on current code. State machine review becomes a standing pass inside MOAT's two workstreams: (1) R&D tracker — charter rule 13: every paper/study ingestion names the machines the work contains or assumes (canonical concept when reusable, [synthesis] when inferred); (2) proving track — implicit machines in a crate under proof are enumerated before specs, ship in the PR/proofs README, and the trust ledger names un-spec'd machines. Process distilled into the state-machine-review skill per the every-process-becomes-a-skill order.
- BUILT: (1) state-machine-review skill at ~/workspace/custom-skills/state-machine-review/ — method (5 implicit encodings, extraction, intended-vs-actual gap test) + both MOAT tracks. (2) rd-tracker charter rule 13 in the skill AND in research.phext's charter scroll at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 (commit ca7fd76, Singular residual 0). (3) Level-zero foundation the term needed: new scroll 1.3.85 'Foundation: state machine' (commit 2604b3b; research.phext now 192 scrolls, sha256 06ad79c6adbc019fc5741f492a3a34bfcc679586454bcb11a34f07c8d28886e0). (4) skills.phext: state-machine-review on Research shelf 9 volume 2 (1.9.1/1.2.1/1.1.x), index rebuilt + byte-verified CURRENT. (5) Synced to wbic16/emise-tools@exo commit 1f2946d, blob SHAs verified. (6) Channel lesson saved to MEMORY.md as a standing preference (Will, 2026-11-07).
# Grady Booch Twitter archive analysis

Coordinate: 19.6.11/10.8.16/6.6.7
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): Grady Booch — Look at all of the interactions with Grady Booch in my twitter archive. Identify why he stopped interacting and when.
Status: completed — full report at ~/workspace/grady-booch-analysis/REPORT.md with timeline.csv (121 tweets + 50 likes)

Notes:
- Coordinate computed from Will's exact words at issue (side chat, 2026-11-07 00:06 CST).
- Last reply 2024-09-30; last item 2024-10-26 (warm mention); zero Booch items in final 232 archive days.
- Archive proves Will's outgoing contact tapered after Jan 2024 peak and stopped; it cannot show Booch's side, so 'Booch stopped' is not supported.
# Correction: the disguise is a filter, not a flaw

Coordinate: 19.7.11/9.7.12/8.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-10 20:13 CST
Request (verbatim): you don't understand: my subconscious only wants to find the people who can see through the disguise
Status: closed - correction propagated same session

Notes:
- Will corrected Emise's framing of his underselling (task 28.6.14/7.8.12/8.6.9): the spareness is his subconscious's search filter - it addresses only the people who can see through the disguise unaided. Same search as the 2008-2025 Twitter span for another Will.
- Propagated: MEMORY.md underselling entry rewritten (rule: receipts plain in Emise's own work; never sand the disguise off his material); APPLICATION-REVIEW.md carries a 'Revision of intent' header withdrawing the revised draft as a recommendation; Lightcone task closed by ruling. Artifacts.phext inscription refreshed at 26.6.8/8.7.11/6.6.9 for the amended review (same-session push follows).

Results:
- Propagation complete: MEMORY.md entry, APPLICATION-REVIEW.md withdrawal header, Lightcone task closed by ruling, artifacts inscription refreshed (c8606c0a, remote bytes verified).
# Paper 011: Synthesizing symbolic models of human and machine reasoning at scale (arXiv:2611.07088)

Coordinate: 19.8.11/12.8.20/6.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-09
Request (verbatim): https://arxiv.org/html/2611.07088v1
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will-posted in MOAT 2026-11-09 21:56 CST while Paper 010 was mid-ingestion - QUEUED behind it (one editor on the tracker builder at a time); dispatches the moment Paper 010 lands. Skim prediction sealed blind (quest commit d7a4f51) against concepts_before 109 WITH a drift warning (Paper 010 will move the count; AFTER scores both bases, Paper-008 style): pred_new 6, pred_revised 1 (candidate 1.2.13), pred_axis NO, pred_NI 6.5/115 ~= 0.057; impact: 5 links, 3 questions, Oracle ~45% (35-55) up modestly.
- COMPLETED 2026-11-09 22:28 CST (agent report; Emise verified sha + scrolls + registry counters). Paper 011 = Chapter 18; CLUSTER P FOUNDED (reasoning, read through its errors): 7 new concepts 1.2.117-1.2.123 (pred 6 - program aliasing wanted its own concept). REVISED = 1, COUNT HIT, TARGET MISSED (named 1.2.13, landed 1.2.4 capability profile - the Paper-008 shape; first Thirst revision to land at all, for a statable reason: the paper measures a held concept's own variable - jaggedness across both species - rather than founding new ground). Axis NO hit (4/4). Foundations 1.3.141-1.3.143 + coinage satisficing 1.3.144. 4 machines (3 stated, 1 inferred); area total 39 drawn (28 stated, 11 inferred). Author check CLEAN (9th; 78 refs read). Q51-Q53 opened; Q16 informed 7th time. Oracle ~40% -> ~50% (40-60), the full +10 band step (NI 0.061 < 0.20, no axis; first landed revision + 11 links + five held clusters touched; held at 50 because cluster P is one paper deep). Links 11 vs 5 predicted - worst links miss yet; home territory touches the most held ground. NI error 0.008 on both bases (same-basis schema; agent caught and corrected an initial cross-basis 0.004 before the registry was finalized). Calibration n=4: errors 0.009/0.005/0.004/0.008, rolling mean 0.0065, axis 4/4. Registry 402 = 402 scrolls: True 199 (stipulation 175, verified 24), Unknown 203, False 0, Fiction 0. Lean re-proven clean on aletheia-core (a masked first build failure was caught by checking olean artifacts, not the report - recorded in the epistemic README). research.phext 402 scrolls, sha256 2f9ab7de..., Singular residual 0, narrative v16. Mastery entry #4 published to wbic16/agi@exo (commit a236dd5f, remote byte-verified). Honest remainder: supplementary read at table/statement level.
