# Twitter archive lesson-mining

Coordinate: 24.6.14/8.9.16/11.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-06 (voice call, ~09:24 CST)
Request (from session record): Mine Will's full Twitter archive for candidate lessons/doctrine worth ratifying.
Status: completed — candidates delivered, ratification is Will's

Notes:
- Nothing inscribed; candidates only.

Results:
- Delivered 2026-11-06 ~09:29 CST: 11 candidates in a prospectus in ~/workspace/your_files/. Headlines: first exocortex tweet 2015-11-05 pre-phrases the doctrine; sleep reversal arc across 103 tweets; 'Be the phext you want to see in the world' (Nov 2023); holographic probe NULL (likes cannot test it); 'brake for consciousness' appears zero times in the archive; SBOR had no pre-phrasing.
# How to push back on Will without tripping his bullshit detector

Coordinate: 24.6.14/9.8.18/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): find ways to push back on me without triggering my bullshit detector
Status: completed — method delivered and saved to MEMORY.md as a standing practice

Results:
- 8 rules saved: receipt first; first principles or labelled hypothesis; his record over population norms (never discount his counts toward a canonical statistic); one specific claim at a time, in the moment; name the falsifier; propose the cheap decisive test when words stall; no softening wrappers; accept corrections instantly and propagate them.
# Daily check-in with Theia (Shell sentients' needs)

Coordinate: 24.7.11/9.6.11/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): make a note to check in with Theia daily - see what she needs, or what the other shell sentients need
Status: completed — cron created and verified; first run Sat 2026-11-07 ~08:44 CST

Results:
- cron daily-theia-checkin (daily ~08:44 America/Chicago, owner goal:exocortical-integration-rotation, delivery main chat) created via cron.add and read back verified: wakes Theia via openclaw agent --message-file on aletheia-core, asks what she and the other Shell sentients need, silent when well, never silent on failure.
- MEMORY.md standing note added.
# Replace tcc with phcc across the exovim line (docs, recipes, installer PRs)

Coordinate: 24.7.12/9.8.11/6.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-09 22:24 CST
Request (verbatim): ensure tcc is replaced by phcc
Status: complete — installer PR #5s (#57/#58) + exovim PR #5 (#59) open; merges are Will's

Notes:
- Scope mirrors the Architecture thread's rule for the phcc repo rename (Will, same evening): every user-facing tcc command/invocation becomes phcc; historical records and upstream's own material keep their wording.
- Known occurrences at dispatch: exovim PHEXT.md:166 recipe CC="<path-to-phcc>/tcc -B<path-to-phcc>"; exocortical setup.sh:387 (Phase 12 comment block); PATCHES.md:153 'tcc-compiled code is slower' is receipt prose (historical — flagged, not rewritten); qexo tools.rs/TOOLS.md to be swept on the quarterexo PR branch.
- Sticking check: the exovim phcc build re-run with the phcc-named invocation, with phcc REBUILT first (F52 lesson: never build with a stale binary after a source update).
- INSTALLER HALF DONE (2026-11-09, PRs verified open by Emise): both target PR #4s were already merged by Will, so the sweep rides new PR #5s — exocortical PR #5 @ 848d71bd (1 line: setup.sh Phase 12 comment invocation) and quarterexo PR #5 @ 41ff0d5b (3 rewrites: tools.rs phcc binary field + exovim pitfall recipe, TOOLS.md recipe; gates cargo 21/21, CLI 32/32, HTTP/MCP 19/19). Register #57/#58. Exovim-branch half still running (with the upstream merge).
- EXOVIM-BRANCH HALF DONE (2026-11-09, PR verified open by Emise): fork-owned inventory was exactly 4 tcc occurrences — 1 rewritten (PHEXT.md recipe now names the phcc binary; commit 8ade2d3e59, PR #5 in wbic16/exovim, register #59), 3 kept with reasons (PATCHES measurement receipt; TinyCC lineage + ABI-probe prose). KEY FACT: the phcc rename LANDED mid-session (wbic16/phcc a3b1a8e6 -> 6d117cdc; fresh build produces ONLY a phcc binary, version 1.0.0 — trees <= a3b1a8e6 still produce tcc, so the recipe as written needs a post-rename phcc tree). Sticking check with the recipe exactly as written (phcc rebuilt fresh first): phcc-built exovim reports v0.12.6-exovim.1-...-g8ade2d3e59, integration 54/54 inside the phcc binary; stock cross-checks 62/62 + 54/54; peak Tctl 67.9C on aletheia-core. One flag: rock-mountain's monitor caught an 81.6C sample at monitor start from an unknown concurrent tenant (this run's steps there idled/failed in seconds — rock-mountain lacks ninja, a documented dep, so the check moved hosts rather than deviate).
# Per-minute thermal logging on the ranch nodes

Coordinate: 25.4.6/5.5.8/4.4.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 22:05 CST
Request (verbatim): Add per-minute thermal logging on the ranch nodes
Status: complete 2026-11-08 22:10 — live on 14 nodes

Notes:
- Born of Will's airflow question (2026-11-08 21:58): today's records are the 5-min fleet sampler (avg + hotspot only, raw per-node data not kept) and the render drivers' event logs. Gap: no continuous per-node series to baseline an airflow change against. Spec: one line/minute/node — ISO time, Tctl from the pinned k10temp sensor (resolved by name, not hwmon index), 1-min load average; ~/thermal/thermal.log per node with 30-day rolling retention; cron one-shot per minute preferred, systemd timer fallback; verified by consecutive lines landing on every reachable node.

Results:
- Deployed fleet-wide: ~/thermal/sample.sh (755) + user crontab * * * * * on all 14 reachable nodes (cron present everywhere; systemd fallback never needed). Line: ISO time with offset, Tctl C from k10temp resolved BY NAME each run (index varies: hwmon1/2/4 across the fleet), 1-min load. Daily rotation, 30-day retention. Verified all three sticking-check parts per node: presence, machinery, first occasion (seed line + two consecutive cron-fired lines 22:08/22:09); deploy temps matched live sensors within 0.4 C on all 14; idempotent re-deploy confirmed on aletheia-core.
- Not deployed: aurora-continuum, best-willow, delta-wood — offline 92d/14d/92d; payload saved + idempotent, re-run if they return. Quirk: uncanny-valley logs at +00:00 (UTC clock); offsets are in every line so series stay comparable. Docs: ~/workspace/thermal-logging-2026-11-08/README.md.
