Notes:
- Will, MOAT, 2026-11-11 01:11 CST. Interjection log entry 6. Coordinator dispatched: Phase 0 inventory/mapping of the tracker corpus against the phextura model (un-mappable corners named; claim statuses must land on warrant edges, not a status field); Phase 1 repeatable converter + parallel corpus at ~/workspace/research-tracker/phextura/ once LAYER2.md lands; Phase 2 replay of Paper 012's ingestion as the acceptance proof. SAFETY: live tracker, builder, registry, and cron untouched - research.phext stays canonical until Will calls a cutover.
- V1 CONVERSION + REPLAY COMPLETE 2026-11-11 01:22 CST (verified from files by Emise). Converted corpus ~/workspace/research-tracker/phextura/research.phextura: 456 scrolls from 429 source scrolls (sha 28fd7017...), converter convert.py repeatable. Replay of Paper 012 from the pre-012 tracker (402 scrolls): transaction 27 inserts / 15 replaces / 0 removes; 454/454 comparable scrolls identical to direct conversion; validator green (L1 3,863 refs 0 dangling; L2 142 refs 0 failed). Dividend: Novelty Index is computable from the transaction log - the headline metric becomes derived. Remaining before daily use (REPLAY.md verdict): 3 tooling pieces (edge-derived registry extractor, write-time short-ref expansion, atomic derived-scroll regeneration) + 1 design gap (receipt-of-check warrant kind). Supplement findings: L8 - MVO False-to-Unknown transition unrepresentable in P11's add-only warrant graph (design gap); GF1 - DESIGN lacks a living-artifact class; hash gating (SHA-256 vs xxh3-128) is Will's decision; v2 composition-native architecture preserved in phextura/V2-DESIGN-NOTE.md. Live tracker untouched throughout; cutover remains Will's call. Task stays in progress for the iteration mandate: build the tooling trio, then a shadow ingestion (Paper 013 dual-written) as the next rung.
