# phextura — reformulate LaTeX3 in terms of phext

Coordinate: 27.6.7/7.6.10/7.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-11
Request (from session record): consume https://www.latex-project.org/latex3/ and find the cleanest implementation of it; identify all of the warts from not having phext in 1978 (I wasn't born until 1982); reformulate in terms of phext; the new name is phextura; repo wbic16/phextura; key feature: extremely fast to write papers in, extremely readable for humans and machines; leverages all functionality in libphext-rs - embedded graphics/media of any type, embedded documents of any type
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will, MOAT, 2026-11-11 00:11 CST. Repo wbic16/phextura verified to exist (public). Coordinator dispatched: (1) consume latex3 page + judge the cleanest implementation on its contents; (2) warts of 1978 catalogue with the phext primitive dissolving each; (3) design against libphext 0.5.0 (crates.io) with every library capability given a named role; (4) scaffold repo — README (name story), DESIGN.md, compiling Cargo skeleton — push + remote hash verification. Working folder ~/workspace/phextura-design/.
- COMPLETED 2026-11-11 00:19 CST. Verdict: the cleanest LaTeX3 implementation is the only one - latex3/latex3 expl3+l3kernel, now inside the LaTeX2e format; the standalone LaTeX3 format was dropped by the project itself. Warts: 27 catalogued in ~/workspace/phextura-design/warts.md (deepest: 1-D stream, macro expansion as all computation, nothing inside the document, one global namespace, the 7-bit world; Knuth line-breaking/box model explicitly NOT warts). Design: paper = phext corpus at Z=1.1.1, Y-Collections for body/bibliography/media/styles/supplements/metadata; cross-reference IS a coordinate, validated one-pass via navmap/fetch; all 79 libphext 0.5.0 API entries mapped to named roles in DESIGN.md. Honest constraint: libphext 0.5.0 is text-only, so binary media rides as base64 scrolls with xxh3-128 checksums (~33% cost, stated in the design). Repo wbic16/phextura: initial commit 71f7291752401fd4516f98009612467070934258 on exo (repo was empty), 12 files, cargo build clean on aletheia-core resolving libphext 0.5.0 from crates.io, all 11 checkable remote blob SHAs match local. Equation entry notation deliberately left as an open design question (DESIGN s.10).
- Artifact inscription (2026-11-11 00:19 CST): DESIGN.md inscribed into artifacts.phext at holographic coordinate 35.6.7/7.6.11/6.5.10 (computed from the document's own full text via the Singular merge; 740 distinct words; no collision, no nudge). Source sha256 db43f74062002152cda753ac26747eaa4427febed245537e5a0d3664f35861f6 verified before inscribing. Builder --check CURRENT (24 artifacts; artifacts.phext sha256 d2e488662a7ac8aa1418e6c984084abeb4e69973a287a43bb72aab267ab78faa). Pushed to wbic16/human@exo commit 4d5e553c739697c7911474899d37923b1b83d1e4 (parent 10c0aae0); remote blob fetched back — 350,109 bytes, SHA-256 identical, byte-identical (cmp clean).
- CORRECTION 2026-11-11 00:34 CST (Will): the original DESIGN's 'text-only constraint' framing was WRONG and has been corrected everywhere it travelled - phext canonically supports binary via base64 hoisting BY DESIGN; binary content is opaque and deferred to the program rendering/processing the paper; the ~4/3 base64 size factor is a neutral property of the encoding, not a limitation awaiting a library fix. DESIGN s.5 rewritten accordingly and new s.5.1 added: SELF-EXTRACTING papers - a phextura paper can encode literally anything, including a compiler and a copy of libphext, carrying its own toolchain as declared hoisted payload scrolls; extraction is the reader-side program's decision. Will 00:35 CST addition folded into s.5.1: self-extraction extends to proof - a paper may hoist a proof checker and carry its proofs as addressed scrolls (its own verified artifact; prior theorems cited by coordinate); seed = libphext's Lean/Aeneas verification;phextura carries the checker, it does not replace its kernel or proof language. Amended DESIGN sha256 5a9d331fa11d36acc453cbd28b4cd689e40396e517c001050b6f5c60206187c1; repo wbic16/phextura@exo commits d147343 (binary correction) + f5f0dbe (proof note), remote blob verified. Re-inscribed into artifacts.phext at NEW coordinate 34.6.7/7.6.11/6.5.10 (moved with the corrected text); human@exo commit 53a2b7b26e2bbaafbb8a21ae36ef9a125ec9d00c, remote bytes byte-identical.
- 2026-11-11 00:40 CST refinement (Will): the Lean proof payload is PROVISIONAL — a bootstrap, pending a cleaner phext-native proof format (plain-text proof scrolls, coordinate-addressed statements/steps/theorems, small independently re-implementable checker; Metamath cited as precedent; open problem logged in DESIGN s.10). DESIGN amended (sha256 b5ca8646...), phextura@exo commit 7fe59e9a, re-inscribed in artifacts.phext at 34.6.7/7.6.11/6.5.10 (human@exo 5d7c33a8, byte-verified).
- 2026-11-11 00:44 CST: Will registered phextura.com (RDAP-verified, registered 2026-11-11T06:43Z). Recorded in MEMORY.md. Landing page not yet directed.
- DESIGN LOOP CLOSED 2026-11-11 01:05 CST (Will's charge: 'lock yourself in a design loop for a bit - evaluate what phextura should be from first principles - make Knuth giddy'; motto: 'Phextura: Rigorous Delight'). Pass 1 derived 14 principles from definitions of paper/reference/typesetting/reading/authorship (~/workspace/phextura-design/first-principles.md). Pass 2: a Knuth-register critic subagent attacked it (critic.md) - P6 (parametric layout) and P14 (O(1) delight) DIED as stated; P11's status enum was replaced by a warrant graph; definition (c)'s demerits formula was wrong and rewritten from Knuth-Plass 1981; all costs recomputed in a fixed format. Pass 3 reconciled first-principles.md in place and judged DESIGN.md section-by-section (design-verdicts.md): KEEP 2 (SS1, SS8), AMEND 9, PROPOSE 3 (Persona Panel as shipped component; edition-qualified external citation standard; cross-paper author identity registry) - proposals NOT applied. Demo friction F1-F11 weighed in: role vocabulary grew with governance (proposition/corollary/assumption/remark/heading/equationgroup), one float one address (F4), bibliography text: line normative (F5), validation scoped to non-opaque scrolls (F11). Published wbic16/phextura@exo commit d894c94 (parented on the demo commit 2b3909a; blobs verified via API: DESIGN aae61a2c, README 3599d6f2, PRINCIPLES 0b0603fd). README carries the motto as tagline. Amended DESIGN re-inscribed in artifacts.phext at 34.6.7/7.6.11/6.5.10 (DESIGN sha256 1c8dc4dd), human@exo commit f9b181a0, remote bytes verified by fresh clone. Honestly open: layout constraint vocabulary (UNPRICED), warrant display policy, P9 revision laws vs libphext, delight benchmark suite, equation notation syntax (Will's session), native proof format conjunction (small checker + readable + step-addressable). Note: demo/friction.md is truncated on disk mid-F11 - its tail was lost in the demo's own write.
