# Review/red-team Will's Lightcone Commons application

Coordinate: 28.6.14/7.8.12/8.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-10 19:46 CST
Request (verbatim): it's my application
Status: closed by ruling - application stays AS SUBMITTED; Emise revision withdrawn (record only)

Notes:
- The org page Will linked (task 39.5.5/5.5.8/6.5.11) is his own Lightcone Commons application; he confirmed it 2026-11-10 19:46 CST.
- Platform application format verified from lightconecommons.com (fetched 2026-11-10): four required sections - (1) What are you working on? (2) What would you do with funding? (3) Who is involved? (4) Logistical details. Free structure for 1-3; live-editable collaborative document; editable any time after submission.
- Evaluator mechanics verified from the same page: screening team tags every application with multiple 1-5 star staff ratings, a Pangram (AI-text) score, and cause-area tags; evaluators produce a funding order + explanations + engagement; applications visible by default to funders, evaluators and direct grantors, who may share externally; evaluators receive a generous LLM token budget and AI tools.
- Individuals are eligible (no 501(c)(3) needed); for individuals, Lightcone determines whether the work qualifies as charitable and provides fiscal sponsorship if so.
- Emise cannot read the application text: the org page redirects to a sign-in wall and no copy exists in memory or files. Review proceeds when Will pastes or exports the text.
- Will sent a screenshot of the submitted application (2026-11-10 19:49 CST). Transcribed and red-teamed against the platform rubric: strengths are voice (Pangram-safe), candor, and a tryable demo link; costs are a receipts-free section 1, no funding amount or milestones, the 'infinite runway' framing arguing against marginal value, an undersold team section, and no cause-area hook for screening tags. One figure flagged to reconcile: application says ~$10K/year self-funded vs the ~$5K/year working burn figure.
- Will reconciled the funding figures (2026-11-10 20:03 CST): recent burn rate $5K/year, ~$15K sunk in total. Review finding 7 updated to resolved and the revised draft's funding section now carries both figures; artifacts.phext inscription refreshed at the same coordinate (new source sha256 7c1e4ded...), pushed as ce647a40, remote bytes verified.
- Will's ruling (2026-11-10 20:13 CST): 'you don't understand: my subconscious only wants to find the people who can see through the disguise.' The underselling is the filter by design; the application stays as submitted and the revised draft is withdrawn as a recommendation. Burn figures reconciled the same evening (recent burn $5K/year, ~$15K sunk). Full propagation record: task 19.7.11/9.7.12/8.7.9.

Results:
- ~/workspace/lightcone-task/APPLICATION-REVIEW.md - full review + paste-ready revised draft in Will's voice; inscribed in artifacts.phext at 26.6.8/8.7.11/6.6.9 (source sha256 91cd98c2...), pushed to wbic16/human@exo as commit 4a1bc8ce, remote bytes SHA-256 verified (da0284ee...).
- Application unchanged by Will's decision; review + withdrawn draft remain at ~/workspace/lightcone-task/APPLICATION-REVIEW.md (artifacts.phext 26.6.8/8.7.11/6.6.9).
# Open PR for phext-notepad emise/ultra-open-fix; review all other branches for rebase/PR needs

