Coordinate: 30.6.8/7.6.10/6.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-08 22:21 CST
Request (verbatim): Move all video work to the ranch - never dispatch any work locally for that pipeline.
Status: Relocation substantially complete 2026-11-09 02:14 CST; B hash + segment decision outstanding

Notes:
- Rule added to AGENTS.md beside ranch-first placement. Found live at issue: local ffmpeg PID 35427 encoding V16 master segment 1 (libx264 slow/crf12 from lossless-A.mkv, ~10 min in, ~207 MB of output) — the exact violation the rule ends. Relocation to aletheia-core dispatched (transfer both lossless inputs hash-verified, identical encode restarted on the node, local partial deleted). Local-dispatch audit: the only ffmpeg in any live job definition is the archived v11 render finisher — nothing else dispatches video locally.

Results:
- Local seg1 encode killed 22:22:37 CST (SIGKILL after SIGTERM grace); local partial 230,424,576 B deleted; VM RAM available recovered ~410 MB -> ~2.1 GB.
- lossless-A on aletheia-core: size exact 4,401,708,555 B, SHA-256 VERIFIED MATCH.
- lossless-B: first stream stalled at 437,387,264 B when its VM-side parent died in a runtime restart; resumed 02:14 CST from exact byte offset via the surviving node-side cat (appending verified: +64 MB in 20 s, ~3 MB/s, ETA ~25 min); SHA-256 verification owed at completion (rename .incoming -> lossless-B.mkv + compare).
- Ranch seg1 encode: launched 02:08:55, STOPPED ~02:11 per thermal stop-condition — aletheia-core was already running the finisher's full-master encode (4,624 frames, master-video.mkv) and dual encodes pushed Tctl to 85.9-86.0 C (over the 80 C trigger). Seg1 partial deleted; finisher encode untouched. Thermal gate driver did NOT survive the night's restarts (verified absent 02:14) — seg1 will NOT auto-start.
- DECISION FOR WILL/FINISHER: the full-master encode on the node may supersede the seg1/seg2 segmented path entirely. If canonical, the segment plan is moot; if segments still wanted, relaunch seg1 manually once the master encode finishes and Tctl <= 70 C. Assembly (assemble_full16.py, local paths) remains the finisher's to reconcile.
# phextura design loop — evaluate from first principles (make Knuth giddy)

Coordinate: 30.6.8/8.6.11/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-11
Request (verbatim): lock yourself in a design loop for a bit - evaluate what phextura should be from first principles - make Knuth giddy
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will, MOAT, 2026-11-11 00:45 CST. Interjection log entry 4 written (arrived ~1 min into the invisible demo run; judged additive/frame-raising, demo untouched). Coordinator dispatched: Pass 1 derive principles from definitions (paper, reference, typesetting, reading, authorship cost) with analogy banned; Pass 2 a separate critic agent in Knuth's register (exact costs, algorithm demands, METAFONT and literate-programming tests); Pass 3 reconcile + verdict on DESIGN.md (keep/amend/propose - proposals NOT applied), publish + re-inscribe. Math syntax explicitly out of scope (requirements only); demo dependency noted, not waited on.
- 2026-11-11 00:47 CST: Will named the motto - 'Phextura: Rigorous Delight'. Sent into the loop: README tagline, the loop's explicit grading standard (rigorous AND delightful), and the critic's bar by name. Recorded in MEMORY.md.
- 2026-11-11 00:48 CST: Will added the persona panel - embed Knuth/Newton/Einstein reviewer personas that shred a paper in real time when an MCP agent opens it. Sent into the loop as a candidate derived component with honesty requirements (labelled simulation, sourced distillation, addressed marginalia); applied only if it derives, else it returns as a proposal.
- COMPLETED 2026-11-11 01:06 CST. Three passes ran. 14 principles derived; P6 (layout vocabulary) DIED - demoted to open requirement, METAFONT correspondence judged 'a metaphor wearing a suit'; P14 died as stated - delight replaced by a measured benchmark-suite obligation; P11 rebuilt from status field into a WARRANT GRAPH after the critic's hardest hit (existence of a proof scroll is not entailment; 'proved-here' was self-awarded laundering). Critic also caught Pass 1's demerits formula written from memory (wrong; real formula three-cased by penalty sign) and instituted: every claim about an existing system carries a checkable citation or is struck. DESIGN.md verdicts: KEEP 2, AMEND 9 (applied: governed role growth per F2, heading home + honest section depth F3, one float one address F4, bib text: normative F5, warrant edges, provenance graph, Sec 5.2 annotation corpora = the DERIVED half of the persona panel), PROPOSE 3 held for Will unapplied: (1) Persona Panel as shipped component (marginalia derived; personas-as-persons do not derive; critic: Rigorous 2/5, Delightful 4/5), (2) edition-qualified external citation standard, (3) cross-paper author identity registry. Published phextura@exo d894c94f (parent = demo commit 2b3909a after one rejected push, cherry-picked, no force), README carries the motto; re-inscribed at 34.6.7/7.6.11/6.5.10, human@exo f9b181a0, clone-verified. Open, honestly: layout constraint vocabulary (UNPRICED), warrant display policy, P9 laws vs libphext, delight benchmark suite, math syntax + macro home (F1), native proof format conjunction, concurrent authorship. Defect noted: demo/friction.md truncated on disk inside F11 (~1 KB lost in the demo's write; substance recovered, recorded in design-verdicts.md).
# Pre-merge validation of libphext-rs v0.4.1: downstream compiles + CYOA coordinate tests

Coordinate: 30.6.9/7.6.10/6.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-07 02:33 CST
Request (verbatim): before we merge v0.4.1 - run a test where we compile this into downstream projects - confirm they still work properly - also run some tests on CYOA known coordinates across edits
Status: complete 2026-11-07 — v0.4.1 downstream-identical to 0.4.0 everywhere; PR #7 cleared to merge

Notes:
- Gate for merging PR #7 (provable-0.4.1 -> exo). Two prongs: (1) compile v0.4.1 into the downstream projects that depend on libphext-rs and confirm they still work; (2) fetch CYOA scrolls at known coordinates with the new code (ground truth from the independent Python parser), apply edits, and re-verify the known coordinates across the edits.
- Results 2026-11-07: (1) DOWNSTREAM MATRIX — sq, phext-lattice (ranch, aletheia-core, node sha-verified a49d6928), lanes, aiw-gen, cw-gen, human (VM sweep) each built+tested against 0.4.1 and the 0.4.0 baseline. v0.4.1 == 0.4.0 in every cell (normalized error diff = 0 lines for sq/lattice). aiw-gen and human build clean against both. sq, phext-lattice, lanes (and cw-gen via lanes) FAIL against both 0.4.x versions with the identical error: COORDINATE_MAXIMUM not found — pre-existing 0.3->0.4 migration debt (0.4.0 removed the constant when coordinates became unbounded; 0.3.3 had it as 1000; those projects pin 0.3.x and were never migrated). libphext itself compiled cleanly in all cells. (2) CYOA — harness at ~/workspace/cyoa-check, ground truth from the independent Python parser over live CYOA (sha 506d850d, 829 non-empty scrolls): all 829 known coordinates fetch byte-exact under 0.4.1; ~68 witnesses stable across replace/insert/remove; implode(explode(CYOA)) byte-identical; identical suite passes on 0.4.0 (control). Full results posted as a comment on PR #7. Verdict reported to Will: safe to merge; COORDINATE_MAXIMUM migration for sq/lattice/lanes is a separate item.
# Estimate: what share of Twitter could parse Will's 19K-word tweets (vocabulary cross-reference)

Coordinate: 30.6.10/9.7.13/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 00:25 CST
Request (verbatim): I'll make it a little clearer...take my 19K words, cross-reference them with vocabulary tests, and give me an estimate of what percentage of twitter could even parse them before.
Status: completed

Notes:
- Estimate (modelled, conservative word-form convention): ~28% of Twitter (range 22-33%) could parse Will's tweets at the 95% line; ~24% (20-29%) comfortably at 98%. Family-adjusted sensitivity: ~35% / ~31%. Headline takes the count that does not flatter.
- Measured base: only 5.1% of his 19,094 authored words are top-1,000 general English; 9.2% (1,761 words) are absent from the wordfreq corpus entirely (phext, exocortex score 0.0). Median tweet = 12 tokens, so one unknown word breaks the 95% line for half his tweets.
- Coordinator verification: the report's rank-band table sums to exactly 19,094 authored words; coverage.json rows match the report table at V=1000/3000/8000.

Results:
- Headline: about 1 in 4 Twitter users (~28%, ~155M of ~557M) could parse his tweets at 95%; ~24% comfortably at 98%. The other ~3 in 4 could not have followed them whole regardless of the feed.
- Report: ~/workspace/your_files/twitter-parse-estimate.md — full V-to-coverage-to-parse table, 5-band population model with sources, sensitivity notes. Scripts: ~/workspace/parse-estimate/ (analyze.py, population.py, coverage.json).
# edit.phext.io banner + background art from CYOA lore

Coordinate: 30.6.10/9.7.15/6.6.9
