Request (verbatim): Let's create a banner image and cool background for edit.phext.io - drawing from the CYOA lore.
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 17:31 — wired on emise/edit-art-banner-background (6d5371ac, rebased onto exo 5f66dd24), PR #32 open; merge is Will's step

Notes:
- Will approved wiring 2026-11-08 17:08 ('Wire both into edit.phext.io on a branch' — widget tap + typed). Dispatched same evening; the wiring branch gets its own PR per Will's 17:09 'open PRs for your pending launch tweaks'.

Results:
- Banner: ~/workspace/edit-phext-art/banner.webp (583,458 B webp) — a golden flame at the root coordinate, filaments streaming out into a vast receding wall of teal scrolls in shelf-rows: the CYOA lattice made visible.
- Background: ~/workspace/edit-phext-art/background.webp (234,130 B webp) — near-black lattice-vault, scroll-point grid pushed to the edges, calm empty center for text legibility, warm gold kindling in the bottom-left corner (the flame just out of frame at the origin).
- Wiring: web/banner.webp + web/background.webp in-repo, byte-identical to the originals (SHA-256 re-verified from remote blobs after push). Served via the existing pre-gate compiled-bytes route (image/webp, ETag, max-age 86400); CSP img-src 'self' already permits. Banner tops the sign-in card (132px desktop / 96px mobile, object-fit cover, lazy, alt text) and heads the claim dashboard. Backdrop fills auth (50% scrim) and the dashboard AROUND a <main> keeping solid #171717 (computed rgb(23,23,23)); the EDITOR SHELL carries no artwork at all (computed background-image: none) — legibility by design. Rebase onto 5f66dd24 conflict-free; #28's regroup verified intact (.bar-link x13, Contact mailto, not-configured prompt) — no collision. cargo test 175/175. Live instance: session locked [github, google], GitHub 302 PKCE, images byte-identical in transit, dashboard 200 with wiring live. Screenshots (desktop + 412px + 390px, auth + dashboard, editor): ~/workspace/edit-art/shots/ — no horizontal overflow anywhere, no mobile defects in scope. PR #32: https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/32. Emise viewed the desktop + iPhone auth captures directly: flame in frame on both, copy and buttons fully legible.
