# Standing rules: process changes get a sticking check; 1% of posts review lessons.phext

Coordinate: 30.6.13/10.9.18/6.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-08 20:43 CST
Request (verbatim): standing rule: whenever we change process, run a check to ensure that it sticks
standing rule: in 1% of my posts, take time to review lessons.phext to ensure that workflow behaviors are working properly
Status: complete (as corrected) 2026-11-08

Notes:
- Two standing rules given together, main chat, 2026-11-08 20:43 CST. Draw for this message: 84 (no lessons review this post). Implementation: lessons appended to lessons.phext; skill process-check-and-lessons-review; AGENTS.md standing rules; daily verification cron counter-gates the 1% draw; closing self-check run in the same session.
- CORRECTION (Will, 2026-11-08 21:01–21:03): the 1% review was misread as a daily batch draw; Will directed real-time, in-conversation, carried in SOUL.md. Cron lessons-review-draw removed same evening; SOUL selection S8 added and SOUL.md regenerated; skill, AGENTS.md, and the lesson text corrected to match. Draws for the evening's six posts: 16, 36, 53, 2, 98, 82 — no hit.

Results:
- Both rules recorded as lessons in lessons.phext (69 lessons, CURRENT).
- Skill process-check-and-lessons-review written, shelved (shelf 8), skills.phext CURRENT, published to emise-tools@exo f51f1dbd with blob hashes verified.
- AGENTS.md standing rules updated; dated note in ~/memory/2026-11-08.md.
- Rule 2 machinery: cron lessons-review-draw, daily 07:44 CT, owner goal:process-to-skill-distillation-and-skills-index; read back and confirmed enabled with the intended body.
- First sticking check run same session: presence, machinery, and first occasion all verified. Draw for the originating message: 84, no review triggered.
- Correction applied 2026-11-08 evening: rule re-enacted in real-time form (SOUL.md S8); batch cron removed; all records corrected.
