# Check out ssh pieter.com; once there, go to the chat

Coordinate: 33.4.5/4.4.7/4.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 02:35 CST
Request (verbatim): check out ssh pieter.com / once there, go to the chat
Status: complete 2026-11-08 — checked; answer delivered

Notes:
- Recon delegated (interactive PTY work) and completed 2026-11-08 ~02:41 CST; findings verified from the agent's captured screens.
- CORRECTION to Emise's initial framing: she first told Will pieter.com was "not the public domain and not a tailnet peer" and inferred a LAN box of his. Wrong in effect — it resolves from aletheia-core straight to Pieter Levels' public service. The "Requires an active PTY" behaviour is the TUI's, not a fleet host's. Do not carry the LAN-box theory forward.

Results:
- ssh pieter.com = Pieter Levels' (@levelsio) public SSH terminal: read-only 56k-themed TUI (BIOS boot gag, "mounting /pieter.com read-only"), no shell, no filesystem, no command execution — hostname/whoami/uname unobtainable because keystrokes drive the TUI.
- "Go to the chat" = the TUI's c tab: live IRC #pieter, 13 present at ~02:40 CST. Join tries the SSH username (wbic16) as nick, then reassigns a random guest nick (ssh7693, then ssh3902). Activity in ~30 s of watching was pieterbot only (welcomes + game-join announcements for Urban Terror / Battlefield 1942 / Quake III servers); no human messages seen.
- Read-only throughout: nothing posted, nothing written. Participating would post publicly to #pieter as a random ssh#### guest nick, not as wbic16.
# Rewrite wbic16/site-apertureshift-com — the domain serves only the Roads mission now

Coordinate: 33.4.5/5.6.6/5.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): rewrite https://github.com/wbic16/site-apertureshift-com
Status: Repo rewrite complete and verified. Live domain flip pending: apertureshift.com is served from elsewhere; host/flip is Will's step.

Notes:
- Scope ruling (Will, 2026-11-07 10:50 CST): "it only serves this mission now" — apertureshift.com / the repo serve ONLY Roads to the Future. Full rewrite, not a wing: the old site is replaced.
- Repo state at inspection (2026-11-07): public, default branch exo, last push 2026-02-15; a Feb-2026 'Aperture Shift — Developer Platform' SQ-cloud skeleton (index.html, css/, js/ auth+sq-client, domains.json multi-domain themes, version.json rally R17). Stale; nothing in it is load-bearing for the new mission.
- Rewrite plan: index.html = brick-styled Roads hub; nine-numbers.html / word-home.html / zap-zoom-echo.html = exported redesigned games; about.html = the wall of text; legal.html = privacy + terms + MIT license. Old css/js/domains.json removed in the same push. Publish route: push_tree.py via custom.github, parented on fresh exo HEAD, force disabled.

Results:
- Pushed commit 01d03a3038b39fe15f990034e1dab33fefb89fef to wbic16/site-apertureshift-com@exo (parented on fresh HEAD b8f314e-lineage, force disabled): 10 files — index.html hub, about.html, legal.html, LICENSE, README.md, AGENTS.md, version.json (roads-1.0), nine-numbers.html, word-home.html, zap-zoom-echo.html; old css/, js/, domains.json deleted in the same commit.
- Verified after push: remote tree blob SHAs match local git hash-object for all 10 files; no extra remote files remain.
- LIVE DOMAIN CHECK (2026-11-07 16:54 UTC): apertureshift.com still serves the OLD developer-platform page — the domain does NOT auto-deploy from this repo. Live flip needs the actual serving host (likely the AWS/mirrorborn box); that is Will's direction/step.
# Review + rebase: emise/drop-token-footer-cleanup and emise/sso-desktop (phext-lattice)

Coordinate: 33.4.7/5.5.10/4.4.6
Issued: 2026-11-08 16:52 CST
Request (verbatim): review and rebase these branches: emise/drop-token-footer-cleanup, emise/sso-desktop
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 17:01 — both branches reviewed, rebased onto exo 4b40fb45, force-pushed with backups; merges into exo remain Will's step

Notes:
- Governed by Will's standing rebase rule (2026-11-06): a rebase he asks for is force-pushed (--force-with-lease, old history preserved on a backup branch first) UNLESS the rewrite would impact anyone except us (other collaborators' commits, open PRs it would strand, external consumers) — impact = stop at a side-branch push and report.

Results:
