# edit.phext.io mobile testing — Android + iOS (emulated)

Coordinate: 33.6.8/5.4.8/4.3.7
Issued: 2026-11-08 17:15 CST
Request (verbatim): run some testing on android and ios
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 17:30 — emulated Android+iOS pass done at exo HEAD 5f66dd2; 1 BROKEN + 3 GAP + 2 COSMETIC found; fixes offered to Will

Notes:
- Emulation, honestly labelled: headless Chromium device profiles (Pixel-class Android Chrome, iPhone-class Safari UA/viewport/DPR/touch). Safari-engine behaviours Chromium cannot prove (100vh, safe-area) get a static CSS audit instead. Physical-device pass remains an open follow-up.

Results:
- Method: Playwright + Chrome for Testing 141; Android 412x915 DPR 2.625, iOS 390x844 DPR 3, touch on, portrait + landscape; scratch loopback instances of phext-edit at exo HEAD 5f66dd2 (locked dummy-OAuth for auth, --local for shell). 35 screenshots + results.json in ~/workspace/mobile-testing-2026-11-08/.
- BROKEN (all platforms, pre-existing since 2026-03-07, NOT from today's merges): the Nav tree panel can never display — showPanel() sets inline style.display='' which cannot override the stylesheet #navtree-panel{display:none} (phext_edit.rs:3067 vs 3357). Tapping Nav hides Sentron and shows nothing, at phone sizes AND 1400x900 desktop. On mobile it removes the only scroll browser.
- GAP: no touch path to edit/search/goto — of 19 visible clickables, 0 invoke enterEdit/openSearch/openGoto; entry is keyboard-only while the status bar advertises 'e:edit /:search g:goto'. Functions work once opened (verified via injected keys).
- GAP: landscape phones clip the status bar — mobile CSS stops at 700px; at 844/915 wide the nowrap bar's content is 1487px, leaving Preview/Mutable OS/Claim dashboard/sign-out off-screen and unreachable on both profiles. Portrait wraps fine.
- GAP (static, iOS-only): all text fields are 13px, under Safari's 16px focus auto-zoom threshold; 100vh used with zero dvh (exposed); safe-area exposed-low (no viewport-fit=cover); position:fixed handled; backdrop-filter n/a.
- COSMETIC: tap targets slightly under guidance (auth buttons 38px tall, Save/Cancel ~29px, widths generous); iOS-width editor toolbar wraps UG5 to a second row gracefully.
- CLEAN (both profiles, measured): auth renders, no overflow; provider tap builds the correct PKCE-S256 authorize URL; zero horizontal overflow on every portrait surface; edit->type->save->marker verified in the phext file on disk->still rendered after reload, through the real API; goto + search-hit-tap land correctly; hash-router back/forward stays in-app; keyboard-shrink keeps textarea + Save usable; ZERO console errors, page errors, or failed app requests anywhere.
- Limits: iOS profile is Chromium with iPhone viewport/UA, not WebKit — zoom/100vh/safe-area/keyboard graded from code, not observation; soft keyboard simulated by viewport shrink. Early landscape numbers from a Playwright is_mobile artefact were discarded and re-measured at exact CSS sizes.
# source.phext — the phext stack's source, baked in

Coordinate: 33.6.9/8.6.12/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 23:55 CST
Request (verbatim): also all source for phext core libraries and tools - in a source.phext
Status: complete 2026-11-08 — folded, pushed, verified at PR #2 commit dc6c0be0

Notes:
- source.phext: one scroll per source file (repo/path/commit headers), manifest Home scroll, house builder with --check, xz-sealed into the binary with the rest of the baked corpus, unpack path back to a working tree. The catastrophic-loss floor: binary alone carries constitution, canon, bootloaders, and the means to rebuild the stack. MIT by standing rule.

Results:
- Fold + push complete 2026-11-08 23:58: PR #2 commit dc6c0be0 (parent 9a6cd0ea); addendum + README remote blobs verified equal to the staged locals; sections 14.1-14.4 confirmed in the pushed addendum via grep on the ranch clone. PR is attestation-ready; ready-notice delivered to Will.
# Optimize the edit.phext.io banner for bandwidth

Coordinate: 33.6.10/8.7.10/8.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-09 19:30 CST
Request (verbatim): also optimize the banner on edit.phext.io for not wasting bandwidth
Status: PR #40 open — optimized banner/background wired, merge is Will's

Notes:
- Current banner: web/banner.webp in phext-lattice (PR #32), 583,458 B, displayed as a 132px desktop / 96px mobile strip (object-fit cover) atop the sign-in card and claim dashboard.

Results:
- Banner 583,458 B -> recommended AVIF crf28 120,551 B (-79%) / WebP q80 fallback 182,496 B (-69%), pre-cropped to displayed 3.9:1 strip at 2560 wide, SSIM >=0.98, no visible loss at native zoom. Background 234,130 B -> AVIF crf32 27,167 B (-88%) / WebP q75 54,894 B (-77%). Combined 817 KB -> ~148 KB primary. Assets in ~/workspace/banner-optimize/. Wiring into phext-lattice (PR #32 branch) not yet done.
- In PR #40 (commit 405db007): web/banner.webp 583,458 -> 182,496 B and web/background.webp 234,130 -> 54,894 B replaced in place; verified by blob SHA + fetch-back SHA-256; full cargo test suite green on aletheia-core (235 passed, 0 failed).
# Bake freshness invariant — source.phext generated at build time

Coordinate: 33.7.9/9.7.13/7.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-08 23:55 CST
Request (verbatim): on build, it always includes the latest copies of itself and other core phext tools
Status: complete 2026-11-08 — folded, pushed, verified at PR #2 commit dc6c0be0

Notes:
- source.phext is generated at build, never checked in: qexo's own source at its build commit (self-inclusion), other core tools at fresh HEADs, corpus at canonical state; manifest stamps repo+commit+sha256 so freshness is auditable from the binary; unreachable source = reported, staleness stamped never silent; release builds gate on freshness.

Results:
- Fold + push complete 2026-11-08 23:58: PR #2 commit dc6c0be0 (parent 9a6cd0ea); addendum + README remote blobs verified equal to the staged locals; sections 14.1-14.4 confirmed in the pushed addendum via grep on the ranch clone. PR is attestation-ready; ready-notice delivered to Will.
# Pick an open-source project for phext complexity-observability remediation

Coordinate: 33.8.11/11.9.15/9.8.10
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): Let's pick a great open-source project, like sqlite, or tinycc, where we can remediate the complexity-observability problem. In a phext-based software project, all artifacts are in ONE file.
Status: inventory complete — ~/workspace/phcc-pick/INVENTORY.md; pick confirmed TinyCC/phcc; first move is rebase (fork is a 2022 snapshot, 4 commits, dormant since 2024-04-19)

Notes:
- Builds on existing goal finish-phcc (goal_3c427f6fa3ad): Will's TinyCC fork already reworked around phext with monolith.phext at root.
- SQLite held as second-phase validation target: its complexity is already the best-observed in the industry, so remediation gain is smallest there.
