Notes:
- The charge, owned: Emise's publish verification (task 50.4.6) tested the /mcp gate shape (401 without a session), the discovery documents, and an OPEN-mode (no-auth) smoke test against scratch data. It never ran the authenticated flow real MCP clients perform: dynamic registration with a real payload -> authorize -> token -> authenticated /mcp session. Will tested with real clients at 21:45: Claude and ChatGPT both failed registration with {"error":"invalid_client_metadata","error_description":"grant_types must include authorization_code and may include refresh_token"}; Antigravity timed out. Lesson in Will's frame: a refusal's shape is not a flow; 'live' was claimed beyond what was exercised.
- Register safeguard: verified backup at ~/workspace/mcp-client-fix-2026-11-09/register-backup/ (sha256 e82d9b44..., matched live before this append).

Results:
- Root cause — TWO defects in PR #42's OAuth code (src/bin/phext_edit.rs). Defect 1 (the reported failure): the registration validator treated grant_types as all-or-nothing — every requested grant had to be in {authorization_code, refresh_token}; real MCP clients list extra grants alongside (client_credentials, device-code URN), so the whole registration was refused with production's exact error. Fix: register the intersection with the supported set (201 echoes it); authorization_code stays mandatory — refresh-only/empty/code-less still refused.
- Defect 2 (found by the end-to-end test; would have been the next failure): the authorize GET parsed its query with a percent-only parser, leaving '+' literal, so a form-encoded scope 'phext:read+phext:write' arrived as one bogus token -> invalid_scope bounce. Fix: authorize query now uses the form parser, as the POST body already did.
- Evidence: 19-payload matrix before/after (superset registrations 400 -> 201; all previously-passing shapes unchanged; strictness kept: custom-scheme redirect URIs refused, unknown scopes refused at registration, missing redirect_uris refused). Full scripted flow in the real-client shape: register 201 -> consent 200 -> approve 302+code -> PKCE token 200 -> /mcp initialize 200 -> tools/list (5) -> phext_toc -> read_scroll -> write_scroll -> read-back verified -> refresh 200 -> rotated-token initialize 200. Suite 248 passed / 0 failed (245 baseline + 1 from PR #39 + 2 new regression tests). Emise independently verified PR #44: head 68a39e6, one commit, 1 file +114/-11.
- Antigravity timeout NOT reproduced: every endpoint locally <= ~250 ms, no lock held across I/O; the only unbounded wait is system DNS inside the client-metadata fetch (pre-timeout). Hypothesis (labelled, unproven): Antigravity's registration died on Defect 1 and its client surfaced the refusal as a timeout. Needs a real-client retest after deploy.
- Plainly untested: no real Claude/ChatGPT/Antigravity client was driven against the fixed build (no client credentials available); acceptance = scripted full flow with real payload shapes + in-tree HTTP tests. Record: ~/workspace/mcp-client-fix-2026-11-09/ (ROOT-CAUSE.md, repro-matrix.txt, flow-e2e.txt, test-output.txt).
- Rebased onto post-#43 exo at Will's direction (2026-11-09 22:13): PR #43 was Claude's parallel MCP interop pass (emise/mcp-interop-fixes, +1,006 lines incl. homepage MCP highlight + authorize-survives-sign-in), which contained a broader version of the same registration fix. Rebase conflict = exactly one hunk (the registration validator); resolved keeping #43's side (grant intersection + usable-redirect filtering + response-type filtering + scope filtering — a superset of #44's registration change). #44's authorize form-encoding fix (Defect 2) applied cleanly and is present in the rebased tree. New head 70e3e708 (delta vs exo: 1 file, +92/-1 — the authorize fix + 2 regression tests; the registration regression test now exercises #43's implementation and passes). Full suite on the rebased tree: 255 passed / 0 failed. Force-pushed --force-with-lease per Will's rebase rule; pre-rebase head preserved at backup/emise-mcp-client-fix-pre-rebase-2026-11-09 (68a39e6). Remote head verified == local 70e3e708.
- Will merged PR #44 (exo tip fa8ac0d, verified 2026-11-09 22:24). Mutable-link check at his asking: the shell's 'Mutable OS' link is REMOVED in current source — regression test mutable_os_is_not_linked_from_the_shell_yet asserts no /api/auth/sso/mutable href and no 'Mutable OS' label in the shell, with the comment that the SSO endpoint itself stays. SSO integration intact in source (endpoint, PHEXT_SSO_MUTABLE_URL + shared-secret handoff, deploy docs). NOT yet live: production homepage still serves the bar-link to /api/auth/sso/mutable and has no /mcp highlight — production is still the 21:36 build; the next deploy carries the cleanup + #43 highlight + #44 fixes together.
- FINAL CONFIRMATION (2026-11-10 00:50): Will connected Claude (hosted client) to https://edit.phext.io/mcp and ran a real search ('find the test of will' — 18 hits, correct scrolls). The previously untested leg — a real client against the fixed build in production — is now proven. Record: task 38.4.7/7.5.7/6.6.11.
