# Estimate: time required to beat OpenAI parameter-golf using phext

Coordinate: 38.5.6/6.6.9/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-10
Request (verbatim): estimate time required to beat this challenge using phext: https://github.com/openai/parameter-golf
Status: completed

Notes:
- Answered in MOAT 2026-11-10 from the repo README/FAQ read in full. Challenge: best LM in a 16,000,000-byte artifact (code + compressed weights), training AND eval each <10 min on 8xH100 SXM, val BPB on fixed FineWeb validation; record to beat is 1.0565 BPB (2026-05-01); new SOTA needs >=0.005 nats at p<0.01 over 3 seeds; official window Mar 18-Apr 30 2026 is closed, so a beat lands as a non-record/unlimited submission or a self-verified record. Phext levers (hypotheses, labelled): coordinate-structured backoff for the winning stack's token-only n-gram memory (the one place format = model), and weights as a field over 9-D phext coordinates (LegendreGPT family, unexplored in 9-D). Phext as mere container/code: no advantage, delimiter bytes count against the cap. Estimate given: ~3 weeks calendar at Will's evenings/weekends pace (~10-15 focused days), ~$400-800 RunPod 8xH100 time (or OpenAI grant, approval latency unknown); ranch cannot run it (H100-specific kernels). Phases: reproduce frontier stack 2-4 days (public, MIT, records ship the winning train_gpt.py), phext prototype + first verdict 3-5 days, margin hunt 1-3 weeks. Odds stated honestly: phext lever carrying the margin ~25-40%; first experiment gives a measurable verdict by end of week 1.
