# Refactor Phext Notepad (PR #5) to consume libphext-cs from NuGet instead of vendored sources

Coordinate: 41.6.9/8.7.12/7.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-09 21:23 CST
Request (from session record): I can't launch phext notepad from this PR: https://github.com/wbic16/phext-notepad/pull/5?overview=true — we should just refactor it to use libphext-cs - I'll get that published
Status: COMPLETE — PR #5 refactored (head f8c45eb, verified open/retitled): vendored sources deleted, app consumes libphext-cs 0.5.0 via PackageReference; build 0 errors, 43/43 equivalence checks vs old code, library suite 60/60. Awaiting Will's NuGet publish for a clean nuget.org restore; first Windows launch unverified.

Notes:
- PR #5 = emise/ultra-open-fix (ultra.phext open fix, stacked on perf-sparse-load / PR #4). The C# WinForms app vendors its own phext sources; the Rust native app already uses libphext-rs 0.5.0. Packages: libphext-cs + Phext.Seal, both 0.5.0. Will is publishing to NuGet himself (register #52 — confirmed in motion 2026-11-09 21:23); verification here packs locally so the refactor doesn't wait on the publish. Watch item: the vendored copy carries the int-coordinate widening — libphext-cs 0.5.0 must support it or the gap gets reported, not papered over.

Results:
- Launch diagnosis: PR #5 code builds clean; the app targets net10.0-windows8.0 — with <=.NET 8 tooling it cannot build/launch; the repo's only prebuilt binary is a stale net6.0 trs.exe, not PR #5 code. No library gap: libphext-cs Coordinate is already int/unbounded; the tree/document/checksum layer is app-side adapter by design. Two flagged behavior deltas: serialization is now a pure function of stored scrolls (vendored code emitted breaks for probed-but-unwritten scrolls), and LeafCount is the exact stored count. Phext.Seal not needed by this app.
# Script the proof-tool install in libphext-rs + wire into exocortical setup.sh

Coordinate: 41.8.7/10.9.12/8.8.12
Issued: 2026-11-07 01:17 CST
Request (verbatim): please add a script to libphext-rs so that we can get those tools installed; also incorporate them into setup.sh in exocortical
Status: complete 2026-11-07 — script committed on provable-0.4.1, Phase 11 live in exocortical

Notes:
- Parent task 47.11.7/12.13.16/12.11.16. Recipe lessons to encode: opam install ./src (the ./ is load-bearing; bare 'src' silently no-ops), charon-ml deps via opam install ./charon, aeneas make SERIALLY (parallel MAKEFLAGS races dune's _build lock), charon built with RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN from its rust-toolchain file (nightly-2026-09-17, host target only), Lean version read from aeneas/backends/lean/lean-toolchain (v4.35.0), set -euo pipefail throughout.
- Closed 2026-11-07. scripts/install-proof-tools.sh committed on provable-0.4.1 (cd18d83; published to the remote branch in the PR #7 stack, mode 100755 verified) and exocortical setup.sh gained Phase 11 running it from its /source/libphext-rs clone (published to wbic16/exocortical exo as 34452c9c). The script codifies the recipe verified manually on aletheia-core; not yet run end-to-end from a clean machine.
# phcc phext capability parity with libphext-rs (C developer library)

Coordinate: 41.10.7/11.11.14/11.10.15
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): make sure phcc has every capability libphext-rs has, so developers can quickly handle phext data
Status: COMPLETE + PUBLISHED (0.5.0) — wbic16/phcc main == exo == 53a15166 (7bd02706 F45 source + 53a15166 phext refresh, on f65e68cc). Publisher verification from a fresh clone: phcc.phext sha256 9cd6bd60…, seal 59799edd…; unpack 613/613 SHA-verified; make test ALL PASSED; parity suite 163,987 checks / 0 failures under gcc with PHEXT_WITH_XZ and 163,987 / 0 under the tree's own phcc; conformance spot 332/333, diverge set exactly [a_pp_018], 0 oracle splits; static cells 3/3 (23 IRELATIVE in .rela.plt in first LOAD, static Lua byte-identical, static phccbox byte-identical, awk 42). Prior 0.4.1 state: COMPLETE + PUSHED @ 8b56ea22.

Notes:
- Phase A parity matrix: ~/workspace/phcc-libphext/PARITY.md (also committed as phext/PARITY.md). 77 capabilities audited from libphext-rs v0.4.1 source: 26 constants, 7 types, 17 Coordinate-surface items, 27 free functions - 77 with C counterparts, 0 gaps.
- Divergences of record: D-2 strict parse returns PHEXT_EFORMAT/PHEXT_ENUMBER where Rust TryFrom panics; D-3 C API byte-oriented, no UTF-8 validation; D-4 map sorted (implode identical); D-5 summary display truncation; D-6 lenient parse wraps like Rust release.
- Phase B: new top-level phext/ dir in a copy of the phcc tree on base 395f5d63 (F1) - phext.h (380 lines), phext.c (1,921 lines, incl. scalar XXH3-128 port), README, tests. Additive only; tcc.h/tccpp.c preprocessor counters untouched - wiring them to the library is the named F3-candidate follow-on, not done.
