- Slice 2 (Wave D7, 2026-11-08; report ~/workspace/phcc-conformance/slice2/REPORT.md; 45 probes: 7 LD run + 38 negative; corpus additive, 333 baseline untouched): (a) long-double depth — pure LD probes three-way byte-identical; F34 TF128<->LD round trips byte-identical to gcc (clang rejects the _Float128 spelling and the f128 suffix: oracle-side gaps); a q-suffix twin probe anchors gcc==clang with the SAME stdout hash (9c88e929...) as gcc/phcc on the f128 spelling, so TF128 numerics are verified three-way and only literal spellings differ (phcc's q-rejection = F34 documented class-(b)); D1 static census 5/5 incl. static LD + static TF128 byte-identical to dynamic and gcc-static. (b) object observables (20-probe subset, tolerances fixed pre-run): sections structurally identical 20/20 incl. .note.GNU-stack; symbol/reloc diffs on 7/20 all classified class-(b) strategy (phcc libatomic helpers, memset/memcpy calls) or oracle-environment (gcc's distro stack protector, gcc's putchar fold); zero class-(a). (c) negative probes: scored set 37 (one oracle-split excluded: void return value, phcc matches gcc); 33 rejected clean; 4 class-(a): const-assignment accepted then segfaulted at runtime (FIXED F38, warning->error, 3 upstream tests2 expectations updated as deliberate fork delta), _Atomic(int[3]) array/function base types (FIXED F39), goto into VLA scope (PQ-26), address-of register variable (PQ-27). (d) arm64 promoted to second gated target: full 333 run cross+qemu — 330/333 three-way agree, diverge set exactly [a_pp_018, b_gnu_015, b_gnu_016] identical to x86_64, Tier C 22/22; one recorded split (a_cmp_004 clang TIMEOUT) proven a load artifact (another resident's ffmpeg at 1567% CPU), re-run byte-identical. En route arm64 blockers F35 (glibc _Float128 typedef) and F36 (_Float128 value assert) fixed. Baseline integrity after all fixes: make test ALL PASSED; slice-1 spot 330/333 with the standing three.
- MSVC manual attestation v1 RUN by Will (2026-11-09, MSVC 19.51.36260 for x64; receipt filed at ~/workspace/phcc-windows/attestation-receipt-2026-11-09.txt): NOT ATTESTED, msvc-agree 3/289 — classified completely as a PACKAGE failure, not a compiler divergence (analysis: ~/workspace/phcc-windows/ATTESTATION-FAILURE-ANALYSIS.md). Census: 289 = 286 run + 3 reject probes; the 3 agreeing probes are exactly the 3 reject probes (never run). 286 mismatches = 282 run failures (every exit code matched; stdout hash only — expected hashes are Linux LF bytes, Windows text-mode stdout is CRLF; proof: expected a_arith_001 stdout_sha256 = sha256('1 1\n') = 3f11ad6b…) + 4 compile-class failures (a_atomic_001–004: MSVC gates C11 atomics behind /experimental:c11atomics, which v1 did not pass); a_pp_018 sits in the 282 and is additionally the known class-(b) __STDC_VERSION__ divergence. Attestation v2 built with the three fixes: CRLF→LF normalization on the captured raw bytes before hashing (byte-wise; comparison is of output modulo the platform text-mode newline translation), /experimental:c11atomics behind a one-time canary (unrecognized-option rejection → v1 invocation for all probes + a receipt note), and a_pp_018 annotated named_divergence in expected.json — reported on its own receipt line ('named-divergences: a_pp_018 (__STDC_VERSION__, class b)') and excluded from the denominator (288 counted; ATTESTED requires all counted to agree). Dress rehearsal without MSVC on the stored conformance oracle outputs (results.json stdout, byte-faithful: 286/286 hashes reproduce): Windows LF→CRLF transform + v1 logic = 0/286 agree (Will's failure shape), + v2 normalization = 286/286 agree; no pwsh on the VM or four ranch nodes, so the .ps1 was syntax-checked by a careful manual pass + delimiter balance. Per Will's direction ('just put the windows attestation tooling in the repo'), v2 ships IN wbic16/phcc at windows/attestation/ (attestation.ps1 + probes/ + expected.json), the v1 receipt + failure analysis under windows/attestation/records/, and a 'Running the attestation' pointer in docs/CONFORMANCE.md — LOCAL commits 2707a31 (tooling) + 3eed671 (records+docs) on tip a3b1a8e6 in ~/phcc-attest-v2/tree on rock-mountain; coordinator publishes (a rename stack is in flight in parallel). Re-run under MSVC is Will's.
